# MemoryBox — SwiftUI MVVM

## Layers

- **View**: layout + bind UI only. No CloudKit, no Core Data fetch, no `MemoryStore` save/load in View body actions beyond calling VM.
- **ViewModel**: `@MainActor` + `@Observable` (or `ObservableObject`). Owns screen state, user intents, calls services.
- **Service / Store**: `MemoryStore`, `CoupleShareService`, `OnboardingStore`. Persistence & CloudKit live here.
- **Model**: pure `struct`/`enum` in `Models/`.

## Rules

- New feature → new ViewModel file. Do not grow `ContentView` with feature logic.
- One screen ≈ one folder under `Views/<Feature>/` + matching `ViewModels/<Feature>/`.
- Extract subviews to their own files when > ~80 lines or reused.
- Prefer constructor injection of services into VMs for testability.
- No `PersistenceController` calls from Views.

## Example

```swift
// ✅ View
struct WelcomeView: View {
    @Bindable var viewModel: WelcomeViewModel
    var body: some View {
        Button("Tạo không gian") { viewModel.createCoupleTapped() }
    }
}

// ❌ View calling store directly
Button("Tạo") { MemoryStore.prepareCoupleShare { ... } }
```

## Migration

When touching a legacy screen that calls `MemoryStore` directly, extract a ViewModel in the same PR if the change is non-trivial. Don't rewrite the whole app unprompted.
